##
    Taking money off, in exact fractions.

    A percentage written as a real would drift; a fraction takes a third off a price
    and means exactly a third.
##

# @summary: A named share taken off a price, held as an exact fraction.
model Discount

    # @summary: What this discount is called.
    string label;

    # @summary: How much of the price it takes off.
    fraction share;

    # @summary: A named discount taking a given share off.
    # @called: what to call it.
    # @taken: the share of the price to remove.
    public function Discount(string called, fraction taken)
        this.label = called;
        this.share = taken;
    end function

    # @summary: What this discount is called.
    # @yields: its label.
    public string function Label()
        yield this.label;
    end function

    ##
        @summary: What is left of a price after this discount.

        @remarks: The arithmetic is exact: a quarter off 2499 is exactly 7497|4 pence, and only
        the last step asks for the real that a price is usually shown as.

        @pence: the price before the discount.
        @yields: what remains to pay.
    ##
    public real function Apply(integer pence)
        fraction kept = 1 - this.share;
        yield (pence * kept).ToReal();
    end function

end model
